    "body": "\r\n> > This specifies existing webkit behavior but I'm not sure it's the desirable one\r\n> \r\n> I suppose in some ways this PR does keep that behaviour the _same_ as it was previously, it just doesn't alter it to match chromium/firefox. So perhaps one other approach than tackling all of precursor origin might be to split that issue out? Or should it be tackled here also?\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean by \"the same as it was previously\". Seems like here you're trying to specify something that's currently not interoperable by aligning the spec on something that's implemented by 1 of 3 engines. I don't think that's a net positive but perhaps I'm misunderstanding what the split would be. ",
