    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T21:29:39Z",
    "body": "I wasn't attempting that, I was more thinking of it in terms of a table of behaviours for different cases, and strictly making each case more interopable / aligned with engine behaviour or the same as before, punting the question of one case which wasn't interopable. But I wasn't correct there on my last comment, writing it out I got the old behaviour mixed up (previously it was secure by accident by making each top level about:blank a secure context), so this is definitely worse.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'll try and investigate different approaches for a better fix here that preserves that behaviour for that case.",
